window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["16"]={"https://theconversation.com/nearly-all-americans-believe-corruption-is-a-problem-but-will-it-decide-the-midterm-elections-295075":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"488f93312ba5dc3bdd1c49e8d2dcefab2ba6e9970c0ba8797bd07a06b15caf1d","read":"https://theconversation.com/nearly-all-americans-believe-corruption-is-a-problem-but-will-it-decide-the-midterm-elections-295075","bytes":181835,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nearly all Americans believe corruption is a problem. But will it decide the midterm elections?","by":[{"n":"Jared Mondschein","r":"Director of Research, US Studies Centre, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-01T19:17:35Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In a politically polarised American electorate, it can be hard to find bipartisan consensus on many issues. Ahead of the US midterm elections, however, there is one thing almost everyone can agree on: concern about government corruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["A record 89% of Americans ",["recently said","https://news.gallup.com/poll/713933/record-high-say-government-corruption-widespread.aspx"]," in a Gallup poll that government corruption is widespread, with Republicans, Democrats and independents all in agreement (ranging between 83-91%). This marks a significant increase from 73% in Gallup’s polling from 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["Out of 132 countries Gallup polled on the question since 2023, only four have recorded higher overall levels of concern: Lebanon and Peru (both 92%), and Ghana and Nigeria (both 90%)."]},{"k":"p","s":["As much as cost of living issues have defined much of the recent campaign rhetoric, a recent Fox News Poll found that ",["concern about corruption","https://electionlawblog.org/2026/a-whopping-88-percent-of-voters-in-latest-fox-news-poll-are-extremely-or-very-concerned-about-corruption-in-government/"]," in government (88%) ranked higher among voters than inflation (85%) or gas prices (83%)."]},{"k":"p","s":["A CNBC survey ",["similarly","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/23/corruption-midterm-election-cnbc-poll-trump.html"]," found government corruption to be the most important issue facing the country, above any concerns about the economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["And according to the ad-tracking firm AdImpact, of the ",["US$11.6 billion","https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/u-s-2026-midterms-money-9.7399429"]," that will be spent in political advertising this election cycle, more than US$275 million has gone to corruption-themed ads – around US$173 for Democrats and US$93 for Republicans."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who do Americans blame?"]},{"k":"p","s":["As much as Democrats point to the unprecedented gifts from foreign governments to the Trump family and the massive expansion of the Trump family wealth during Donald Trump’s second presidential term, Americans are by no means exclusively blaming the Trump administration for corruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the Brennan Center for Justice, a voting rights organisation, ",["asked","https://www.brennancenter.org/media/15709/download/corruption-survey-toplines-2026-06-01-final.pdf?inline=1"]," a representative sample of 2,000 Americans this year whether certain individuals or institutions were corrupt, respondents had negative views across the political spectrum. These included view about Congress (85%), Trump (68%), Joe Biden (63%) and the Supreme Court (62%)."]},{"k":"p","s":["And when asked whether this is a problem driven by individuals making unethical choices or a problem “deeply embedded in the institutions of the US government”, about two-thirds of respondents chose the latter. Only 7% said they were not concerned about corruption influencing elected officials."]},{"k":"p","s":["This does not appear to be a new phenomenon. Levels of trust in American politicians, political parties, news media, government institutions and even the “American people” have been ",["declining","https://news.gallup.com/poll/715361/trust-federal-government-sinks-new-depths.aspx"]," since Gallup began polling on the issue in the 1970s. And they’ve hit record lows in recent years. While 86% of Americans trusted the American people in 1976, today barely half do."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adding further nuance to this issue: Gallup also ",["highlights","https://news.gallup.com/poll/713933/record-high-say-government-corruption-widespread.aspx"]," the significant gap between American perceptions of corruption in government (89%) versus corruption in business (71%). The survey says few countries have gaps this large."]},{"k":"p","s":["And, interestingly, this public perception of corruption does not trickle down to local politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["another survey by YouGov","https://yougov.com/en-us/articles/55653-three-quarters-americans-think-most-or-many-elected-officials-are-corrupt-september-25-28-2026-economist-yougov-poll?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"]," many more respondents deemed US senators and representatives to be corrupt (75%) than mid- or low-level government workers (39%)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This gets to an important reason why such high levels of distrust in institutions have not led to more unrest: Americans still appear to have trust in their local governments."]},{"k":"p","s":["And this has largely not changed since Gallup first polled on the topic more than 50 years ago. Today, two-thirds of Americans trust their local government, which is actually slightly higher than the 63% who did in 1972."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the whole, Americans also retain trust in the ",["ability of elections","https://statesunited.org/resources/voter-confidence/"]," – like the midterms – to act as political circuit breakers."]},{"k":"h","s":["What about the midterms?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Candidates running for office this year have taken note of the deep voter distrust in Washington elites, parties and institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["One need only watch a few of the many viral political ads this campaign to see a well-worn script: candidates blame Washington insiders for corruption and other issues, while touting their local bona fides."]},{"k":"p","s":["It should come as no surprise that many candidates are eschewing party labels altogether, often going so far as to ",["criticise","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/10/28/politics/video/turek-pitches-swing-voters-digvid"]," ",["their","https://www.reuters.com/world/us/most-republicans-tight-midterm-distance-themselves-trump-reuters-review-finds-2026-10-07/"]," own party."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this is not the first time politicians of all stripes have appeared keen to distance themselves from the ruling class, and from political insiders viewed as corrupt and detached from the everyday realities of most Americans."]},{"k":"p","s":["After all, with the exceptions of Biden and George H.W. Bush (both former vice presidents who served under popular two-term presidents), every US president of the last half century has come to the Oval Office with fewer than five years of experience in Washington – if any."]},{"k":"p","s":["Americans have largely been against Washington insiders for decades – particularly when economic anxiety is high."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet what’s different in this year’s midterm elections is how many are trying to fuse corruption with that economic anxiety. Not since the 2006 midterm elections has corruption been such a prominent theme in an election."]},{"k":"p","s":["James Talarico, the Democratic hopeful for the Senate in Texas, has ",["said","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/james-talarico-faces-trump-dueling-texas-rallies-elections-final-days-rcna605629"]," on the campaign trail, “we have an affordability crisis because we have a corruption crisis”."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in Georgia, Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff ",["routinely tells voters","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xnj-2yfL13U"]," “corruption is why things don’t work for ordinary people.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["These Democratic efforts follow similar efforts by Republicans to portray Democrats as the more corrupt party costing American taxpayers money."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elon Musk’s Department of Government Efficiency, for instance, sought to target what it called “ ",["waste, fraud and abuse","https://fortune.com/2026/10/22/federal-judge-ruling-doge-opm-broke-law-access-sensitive-data-elon-musk/"],"”. And Republicans in Minnesota have ",["highlighted","https://www.foxnews.com/politics/he-had-years-to-stop-this-gop-lawmakers-blast-walz-over-massive-minnesota-fraud-scheme"]," a welfare-fraud scandal that essentially forced Democratic Governor Tim Walz to abandon his plans for a third term of office."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s unclear whether these sorts of accusations will inspire the political backlash that other issues – namely abortion, immigration and the economy – have in past elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, Democrats do have one advantage in the midterms. They are currently seen as the preferred party ( ",["by 10 percentage points","https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fox-news-poll-cost-living-concerns-weigh-gop-midterms"]," in recent polling) to fight corruption. This explains why they are spending nearly twice as much on ads about corruption than Republicans."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, should Democrats be successful and take control of Congress, they will be expected to act on this issue, and not just become part of the ongoing problem."]}],"chars":6300},"https://theconversation.com/johannesburg-and-medellin-what-south-africa-can-learn-from-colombia-about-fixing-a-broken-city-292092":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"f03588ef33dadbfc01ee35a19d2329d223426d18b2f75e1be488175f92d9e072","read":"https://theconversation.com/johannesburg-and-medellin-what-south-africa-can-learn-from-colombia-about-fixing-a-broken-city-292092","bytes":180747,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Johannesburg and Medellín: what South Africa can learn from Colombia about fixing a broken city","by":[{"n":"Ivor Chipkin","r":"Associate lecturer, University of Pretoria"}],"pub":"2026-09-29T06:17:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The city of Johannesburg – South Africa’s largest – is increasingly unable to perform even its most basic functions, such as providing clean water and electricity and maintaining its roads and the safety of its citizens. It has the symptoms of a broken city: deteriorating financial controls, a swelling wage bill, unstable coalitions and rapid mayoral turnover."]},{"k":"p","s":["Describing these problems, however, does not amount to a diagnosis. And no project of renewal can begin without a diagnosis."]},{"k":"p","s":["My ",["research","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=EicVU1gAAAAJ&hl=en"]," over the last three decades has focused on the challenges of government in post-apartheid South Africa. I also spent years working on local government, both as an activist opposed to apartheid and as part of the team that developed the ",["White Paper on local government in 1998","https://www.cogta.gov.za/cgta_2016/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/whitepaper_on_Local-Gov_1998.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a ",["recently published paper","https://nsi.org.za/publications/the-crisis-of-johannesburg-an-agenda-for-institutional-reform/"],", The Crisis of Johannesburg: An Agenda for Institutional Reform, commissioned by an independent think tank, the Centre for Development and Enterprise, I explored the governance of the city, why it has deteriorated so seriously over the last ten years and what might be done about it."]},{"k":"p","s":["I argue that the conventional diagnosis – that Johannesburg’s crisis is simply one of poor governance and weak leadership – is insufficient."]},{"k":"p","s":["The deeper problem is institutional and legal. I argue that the problem with the city, like other municipalities in the country, is that the administration only exists in name. All power lies with the council. The city manager has no inherent authority to hire staff or to make operational decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["In devising solutions I draw on the experience of Medellín, Colombia’s second largest city. For a long time ",["it was officially the deadliest place in the world","https://architectureindevelopment.org/news/49"],". Its recovery depended on a city government that could combine security, investment and capable utilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Johannesburg’s recovery will depend on applying a similar approach. Its utilities – City Power, Johannesburg Water and the waste management service provider Pikitup – must get real operational autonomy. Johannesburg now has to decide whether its utilities will be used for rebuilding the city, and whether it is prepared to confront the political and criminal networks that will resist this."]},{"k":"h","s":["The emergence of a mega-city"]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the past 30 years Johannesburg has developed into a large metropolitan entity absorbing other towns and municipalities. The idea was to create a new city as a metropolitan authority that could pool resources across historically unequal areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["The city was also restructured through the ",["iGoli 2002 plan","https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/server/api/core/bitstreams/cd89c5a2-6666-51c3-a26b-faf44236b04a/content"],". Major service functions were reorganised into corporatised entities."]},{"k":"li","s":["The electricity department became City Power, a company wholly owned by the City."]},{"k":"li","s":["The water department became Johannesburg Water. In its early years it was managed by the French water company ",["Suez-Lyonnaise des Eaux","https://www.suez.com/en/north-america"],"."]},{"k":"li","s":["Pikitup was established as the municipal company responsible for waste collection and cleaning."]},{"k":"p","s":["The idea was that these functions were large technical businesses and needed to be run as such. They required dedicated management, clear responsibilities and accountabilities, technically competent employees and financial discipline."]},{"k":"p","s":["These reforms were controversial from the beginning. The ",["South African Municipal Workers Union","https://samwu.org.za/"]," and the not-for-profit campaign group the ",["Anti-Privatisation Forum","https://apf.org.za/spip.php?article2"]," opposed them as concessions to neoliberalism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Johannesburg never settled how the utilities should relate to the city administration in terms of governance and decision making over finances. The result has been a hybrid arrangement. The utilities are expected to operate like businesses. But many of the key functions on which a business depends are centralised and politically contested. Billing, treasury, cash allocation, staff appointments, procurement and capital expenditure were never insulated from wider municipal instability."]},{"k":"p","s":["The utilities were autonomous enough to fragment responsibility, but not autonomous enough to protect their own operations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is political."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Municipal Systems Act","https://www.gov.za/documents/local-government-municipal-systems-act"],", passed in 2000, created the position of municipal manager, appointed by the council. But the act did not provide a clean separation between political direction and administrative authority. Councils remain deeply involved in appointments and senior administrative arrangements. Executive mayors, mayoral committees, boards and entity executives all have roles, but accountability is dispersed."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the coalition period, which began in 2016 when the African National Congress lost its majority in the city council, the administrative space has weakened further."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the past decade the city has too often been divided between coalition partners. Each has treated departments or entities as personal areas of influence. This has affected appointments, boards, procurement and operational decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The result is the conversion of municipal institutions into political assets. Utilities that should be technical service institutions have become sites of patronage, rent extraction and factional control."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is where Medellín offers a useful point of reference."]},{"k":"h","s":["What fixing problems took in Medellín"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 1980s and 1990s ",["the city","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/591a33ba9de4bb62555cc445/t/5e794bff68138043312d9be2/1585007620409/Corburn+et+al+2019_transform+Medellin+City+for+Life.pdf"]," became known as the most violent in the world. By 2013, however, ",["it had come to be recognised as the most innovative","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-21638308"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medellín’s recovery required the restoration of public authority in areas where powerful criminal and armed cartels had displaced the state. The state had to become visible and useful where it had been absent or predatory."]},{"k":"p","s":["The municipal utility, ",["Empresas Públicas de Medellín","https://www.epm.com.co/"],", was central to this process. It supplied electricity, water, sanitation and telecommunications. It generated revenue, maintained infrastructure and helped finance the city’s broader investment programme. It showed that a public utility can be commercially disciplined and socially useful at the same time. It can provide services effectively, generate resources for the city, and support investment in poorer areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is the main lesson for Johannesburg. Utilities are a problem if they are poorly governed and politicised, and if they don’t have protected cash flows, competent management or clear authority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medellín’s experience shows that utilities can be part of the renewal of a city if they have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["shareholder compacts with the city"]},{"k":"li","s":["billing and treasury rules that specify how revenue is collected and how cash is allocated"]},{"k":"li","s":["performance targets that are public and measurable"]},{"k":"li","s":["protection from political interference in appointments, operations and procurement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vested interests will resist change"]},{"k":"p","s":["This will not be a purely administrative exercise. Renewal in Johannesburg will confront interests that benefit from the current disorder. Some of these interests are inside formal politics. Some sit on boards, or in entities, departments and supply chains. Some operate through contractors, local brokers or criminal networks."]},{"k":"p","s":["A reform programme that threatens these arrangements should expect resistance. That resistance may take the form of litigation, obstruction, leaks, disinformation, labour disruption, sabotage of infrastructure, intimidation of officials, and violence around worksites and depots."]},{"k":"p","s":["Johannesburg’s recovery will require both professionalisation and enforcement. It will need a professional and relatively autonomous administration, but also a policing strategy capable of protecting infrastructure, officials, contractors and communities from organised disruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["This does not mean militarising municipal government. It means recognising that service delivery depends on public authority."]}],"chars":7526},"https://theconversation.com/labours-immigration-dilemma-with-social-care-exceptions-the-party-is-trying-to-have-it-both-ways-295909":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"6a084970f25961edc032c71d7b1208ea0de5f837e786d50b49a506b87286298d","read":"https://theconversation.com/labours-immigration-dilemma-with-social-care-exceptions-the-party-is-trying-to-have-it-both-ways-295909","bytes":182507,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Labour’s immigration dilemma: with social care exceptions, the party is trying to have it both ways","by":[{"n":"Erica Consterdine","r":"Senior Lecturer in Public Policy, Lancaster University"}],"pub":"2026-11-06T12:05:15Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Home Secretary Shabana Mahmood’s headline announcement on immigration centred on how long someone must spend in the UK before they can be granted indefinite leave to remain (ILR). She said this period will double from five to ten years – but social care workers will be exempt. This proposal was widely expected, but exempting social care workers is a U-turn for the government."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["proposals","https://theconversation.com/topics/immigration-411"]," were met with a ",["mixed response","https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/02/shabana-mahmood-softens-immigration-plans-cabinet-backlash-leave-to-remain"],". Some on the left said the qualifying period is too high, while others on the right claimed the plans were too lax on immigration by exempting care workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many migrants came to the UK on the understanding that five years of lawful residence would provide a path to settlement. So the government’s decision to retrospectively change those terms raises serious questions about fairness, trust and the legitimacy of immigration policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK is now moving towards one of the toughest settlement and naturalisation systems in Europe. In fact, this direction is more readily associated with the political right than a Labour government that presents itself as committed to equality, workers’ rights and social justice. So where are we now with immigration policy, and what does this shift tell us about British politics?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Years of talking tough"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tough naturalisation requirements come off the back of 16 years of restrictive rhetoric on immigration across the political spectrum. From 2010, the Conservative-led coalition government set a pledge to ",["reduce net migration","https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/sn05829/"]," from hundreds of thousands to the tens of thousands. And since then, successive administrations and opposition parties have attempted to outflank each other on tough immigration talk."]},{"k":"p","s":["The last Conservative government lurched towards ",["nativist, exclusionary rhetoric","https://www.kcl.ac.uk/suella-bravermans-talk-of-a-refugee-invasion-is-a-dangerous-political-gambit-gone-wrong"],", and ",["draconian policy proposals","https://theconversation.com/hostile-environment-brexit-and-missed-targets-14-years-of-tory-immigration-policy-231407"]," in a bid to ",["outmanoeuvre Reform UK","https://www.politico.eu/article/nigel-farage-is-spooking-the-conservatives-again/"],". The result has been to keep immigration high on the public agenda (though with ebbs and flows following Brexit and COVID)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet despite the tough talk, the combination of an economy that needs migrant labour as well as humanitarian schemes for citizens of ",["Hong Kong","https://www.gov.uk/british-national-overseas-bno-visa"]," and ",["Ukraine","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/support-for-family-members-of-british-nationals-in-ukraine-and-ukrainian-nationals-in-ukraine-and-the-uk"],", took net migration to the ",["highest level","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3degx4029ko"]," on record. This was in 2023, the year before the Conservatives left office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Critically, while previous governments talked tough on immigration, Brexit left major shortages in the labour market, especially in some of the low-paid jobs that many Britons do not want to do. As a result, a number of policy schemes were introduced to plug these gaps, including the ",["health and care visa","https://www.gov.uk/health-care-worker-visa"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This scheme proved popular, resulting in ",["106,000 visas","https://migrationobservatory.ox.ac.uk/press/social-care-sector-continues-to-drive-demand-for-overseas-workers-as-new-data-shows-public-sector-roles-dominate-work-visas/"]," being issued to social care workers (the figure excludes their dependants) in 2023. But since then, more scrutiny on sponsors and the decision to stop dependants coming to the UK on this visa have led to ",["sharp declines","https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/immigration-system-statistics-year-ending-june-2026/why-do-people-come-to-the-uk-work"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labour has long been ",["dogged on immigration","https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-319-64692-3"],". The party spent most of its years in opposition apologising for apparent mistakes made in office over the managed migration programme. This was a series of policies that resulted in one of the most ",["expansive immigration policies in Europe","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/bp.2013.19"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["And ideologically, immigration has always been a ",["headache for Labour","https://theconversation.com/labour-governments-have-always-struggled-with-immigration-heres-what-keir-starmer-could-learn-from-them-256737"],". Like other social democratic parties, Labour is torn between its protectionist trade union roots, which favour tighter borders, and its rights-based tradition of protecting migrants."]},{"k":"p","s":["The dilemma is further complicated by Labour’s neoliberal turn since the Blair era, which saw ",["globalisation as inevitable","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/1369183X.2015.1045711?casa_token=EIUqjkoIEykAAAAA:wlOZ9r_11jrEGFwCSCX9mZjGC1J8f_Qorr2ocJI_o43BtPb966Lx8ZcKnPU8dE2Xwythq7erEcvl"]," and embraced flexible labour migration as a way of controlling inflation. In short, Labour has been complicit in deepening a labour market that depends on on migration for its workforce, while using the “secure borders” rhetoric."]},{"k":"p","s":["These ideological tensions are reflected in the make-up of both the Labour party and its electorate, bringing together members and constituents with competing values and priorities – the “beer drinkers” and the “wine drinkers”. And they are precisely why the new rules contain a mixed bag of restrictions and concessions on social-care visas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Andy Burnham’s government has faced this tension head on, with many in the party lambasting Mahmood’s pursuit of high thresholds for naturalisation. Prominent figures including Housing Secretary ",["Angela Rayner","https://uk.news.yahoo.com/angela-rayner-condemns-shabana-mahmoods-065347371.html"]," had accused Mahmood of “pulling the rug” from underneath people. This intra-party tension resulted in the decision to exempt social care workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Policies that increase immigration are never generally vote winners. But social democratic parties have a choice whether to keep quiet on the issue, accommodate pressures from the right, or attempt to walk a middle ground of selective immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Former prime minister Keir Starmer was accused of echoing ",["right-wing rhetoric","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/12/keir-starmer-defends-plans-to-curb-net-migration"]," and produced the restrictive ",["white paper","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/restoring-control-over-the-immigration-system-white-paper"]," from which the new policies stem. In practice, Labour’s approach is built on contribution-based residency – the more you earn the longer you can stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["So far, Burnham has largely sailed the same ship, maintaining Mahommod as home secretary and changing little of the direction on immigration. Yet his recent comments on ",["humanitarian schemes","https://theconversation.com/should-andy-burnham-be-relentless-on-small-boat-crossings-experts-react-288979"]," and reopening the debate on ",["free movement","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8e36kyk1qx5o"]," suggest that the tide might be beginning to turn. Mahmood’s U-turn on social care workers might be part of this shift."]}],"chars":5241},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"b5bd2a238062fc817cbd7a84f06b77ba49075f2b2ff4017ce5cb7685b515b009","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/mali","bytes":65517,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Mali travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-10T14:24:11+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Mali"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the whole of the Mali due to the unpredictable security conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Mali, you should leave immediately by commercial flight if you judge it safe to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not try to leave Mali by overland routes to neighbouring countries as this is too dangerous. This is due to terrorist attacks along national highways."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist group Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) has implemented blockades on key routes throughout Southern and Western Mali, including the capital city of Bamako. These blockades are targeting fuel trucks and are enforcing checkpoints for individuals attempting to pass through them. Attacks can occur at any time."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of kidnapping and criminal activity across Mali, including in the capital, Bamako."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to remain in Mali, you do so at your own risk. You should have a personal emergency plan that does not rely on the UK government."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more detail see ",["Fuel shortages","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/safety-and-security#fuelshortages"]," and ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/safety-and-security#Terrorism"]," in Mali in the Safety and security page."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national already in Mali, either resident or visitor, carefully consider your presence there and the risks you take by staying."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Support for British nationals is severely limited in Mali, especially outside Bamako."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not rely on FCDO being able to help you to evacuate in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Mali and need emergency help from the UK government, contact the ",["British Embassy in Bamako","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-bamako"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK, who choose to travel despite FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Mali’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Mali set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Malian Embassy in Europe","https://www.amba-mali.be/"],", which covers the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Mali, your passport must be valid for the duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Mali. The application and payment process is now fully online via the ",["Malian Ministry of Foreign Affairs website","https://diplomatiemdc.gouv.ml/vitrine/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["An entry permit will be issued electronically once approved. There is no need to send documents to the Malian Embassy in Brussels, which covers the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Mali, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Mali","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/140/mali#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," guide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Mali","https://douanes.gouv.ml/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get an export permit from the Ministry of Arts and Culture to take any cultural or archaeological objects out of Mali. You can get this from the director of the National Museum."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Mali"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Mali."]},{"k":"p","s":["Several terrorist groups operate in Mali, including Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) and Islamic State Sahel Province (ISSP). Whilst the regions most affected by terrorist activity are central and northern Mali, JNIM has increasingly conducted attacks in southern Mali and has the capability and intent to target the capital, Bamako."]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in Mali has deteriorated amid an upsurge of terrorist attacks following the December 2023 withdrawal of the UN peacekeeping mission. Terrorists have increasingly attacked military bases and personnel, sometimes including foreign military personnel, as well as government and official buildings, including in Bamako. Such attacks often lead to the deaths of soldiers, civilians and others. Attempts to carry out similar attacks remain very likely."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist group Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) has implemented blockades on key routes throughout Southern and Western Mali, including the capital city of Bamako. These blockades are targeting fuel trucks and are enforcing checkpoints for individuals attempting to pass through them. Attacks can occur at any time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care during elections and public holidays, and periods of national or religious significance. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities, including by complying with access restrictions imposed by authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate and occur at any time, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["national infrastructure"]},{"k":"li","s":["military sites and institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["government and official buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["international institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs, including airports and major roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["international businesses, including mining companies and operations"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites and places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres and crowded places"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, restaurants and bars"]},{"k":"p","s":[["See also road safety","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/safety-and-security"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 4 July, further coordinated attacks targetting military installations were carried out across multiple cities including Anefis, Aguelhoc, Gao, Sevare and Kenioroba"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 25 April 2026, a series of coordinated attacks occurred in multiple locations including Kidal, Gao, Kati, Severe and in the vicinity of Bamako International Airport (leading to the airport’s temporary closure)"]},{"k":"li","s":["since September 2025, there has been an increase in attacks targeting fuel convoys in Mali, particularly in southern and western Mali"]},{"k":"li","s":["in June 2025, JNIM claimed to kill more than 150 soldiers, in multiple attacks targeting military bases in Boulkessi, Timbuktu and Mahou"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March and May 2025, there were two separate attacks against a police station and a military base which damaged vehicles and infrastructure in Kati, approximately 15km from Bamako city centre"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February 2025, a roadside bomb killed two people and injured others in a convoy that was travelling on the road linking Kati to Soribougou"]},{"k":"p","s":["This continues a historical trend of terrorists attacking military bases and personnel, sometimes including foreign military, often leading to the deaths of soldiers, civilians and others."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a very high threat of kidnapping by al-Qa’ida and Islamic State-aligned groups in Mali. JNIM and ISSP operate throughout Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso. JNIM, in particular, has previously conducted kidnappings from all parts of Mali, including in urban areas and the capital, Bamako. In 2025, there was been an increase in kidnaps in Southern and Western Mali."]},{"k":"p","s":["A number of foreign nationals have been kidnapped in Mali in recent years, by Al-Qaeda and Islamic State affiliated groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are working or travelling in Mali, be aware of the very high threat of terrorist kidnapping. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times, including when travelling and in crowded public places, including camps for displaced people, religious gatherings and places of worship, markets, shopping areas and places frequented by westerners like hotels, bars, nightclubs, restaurants and transport hubs. You should avoid regular patterns of travel and aim to only travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is to not make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 24 May 2021, the vice-president, Colonel Assimi Goïta, detained the transitional President Bah N’Daw and Prime Minister Moctar Ouane, along with other members of the transitional government. Goïta was sworn in as head of state in June 2021. Presidential elections, originally scheduled for February 2024, were postponed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political unrest is an ongoing risk. Regular, large and at times violent protests have taken place in Bamako, with burning of tyres and clashes with the police. Police have responded with tear gas and small arms fire. Deaths and injuries have been reported."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local media and stay away from all large gatherings and political demonstrations. Avoid any blockades set up by the police and security forces. Keep several days’ stock of food and water in of case disturbances. You can monitor daily developments in English through the BBC World Service (88.9 FM in Bamako)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security incidents between and within communities continue in many parts of the country, most notably in Mopti and Segou regions. In some instances, terrorist groups have become involved in these conflicts. Groups operating in the centre, north and north-east sectors use landmines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of violent crime is high, especially in the capital Bamako and southern regions. Be alert to the risk of street crime, armed robbery and kidnapping."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the northern border areas, bandits and smugglers may attack travellers, especially after dark. There have been instances of authorities asking for small payments from foreigners and Malians."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not walk alone at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid isolated areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["take particular care when using ATMs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep copies of your passport’s photo page and your visa or entry stamp in a separate place from the original in case your passport is stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping by criminal groups is widespread across Mali. There has been an increase in kidnappings of western nationals and gangs operate throughout Mali, including in Gao and Keyes regions. There is a possibility that criminal groups could sell people they kidnap as hostages to terrorist organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release. You should avoid regular patterns of travel and aim to only travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of carjacking and kidnap across the country. If you are travelling against FCDO advice, beware of the threat to your vehicle and get advice from a security company or personal sponsor. There have been reports of vehicles driven by foreign nationals being vandalised."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk of attacks:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take professional security advice before you travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel in pre-arranged transport with trusted operators"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep doors locked and windows shut while in the vehicle"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave the scene as quickly as possible if your vehicle is targeted"]},{"k":"li","s":["report any incident to the police"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mali is a secular country, but the people are predominantly Muslim. The country’s laws and customs are very different to those in the UK. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not offend religious beliefs, especially during Ramadan or in religious areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["French is the official language in Mali and not many officials or healthcare workers speak English. You may have difficulty communicating if you cannot speak any French. Make sure you can use translation apps in case of an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a foreign national, you must carry ID such as a passport. You could face difficulties with security checks if you do not have the original document on you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take pictures of military or government installations. Always ask permission before taking photographs that include local people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Commercial disputes"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in or connected to a business or civil dispute in Mali, the Malian authorities may detain you, prosecute you or prevent you from leaving Mali until the matter is resolved."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Homosexuality is illegal in Mali. In December 2024, Mali’s National Transitional Council promulgated a new Penal Code which criminalises the promotion or participation in consensual same-sex relationships. The legislation introduced penalties of up to seven years imprisonment and fines of up to 500,000 francs."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased risk of violence and threats, such as blackmail and intimidation, against anyone being thought to be part of the LGBT+ community or perceived to be supporting their rights. There have been arrests for ‘immoral behaviour’, and LGBT+ individuals have experienced physical, psychological, and sexual violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Mali, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Mali. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police checkpoints are common throughout Bamako. Always keep vehicle and personal identification documents with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Approach security checkpoints slowly and follow instructions. There have been incidents late at night where people dressed as policemen have demanded money from drivers in Bamako. Ask to see identification and get a receipt for payment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exercise caution and do not resist demands if you feel threatened or in danger."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions in Bamako are difficult during the rainy season from June to October. Roads outside Bamako are often damaged and dangerous. Other road users may drive unpredictably."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks on major roads and transport routes by terrorists are increasing across the country, including through the use of landmines and other explosive devices. This is particularly the case in areas where terrorist groups are operational and near border areas, including the roads in northern and eastern Mali."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist group Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) has implemented blockades on key routes throughout Southern and Western Mali, including the capital city of Bamako. These blockades are targeting fuel trucks and are enforcing checkpoints for individuals attempting to pass through them. Attacks can occur at any time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take all necessary safety precautions, especially outside of main urban areas, have confidence in your security arrangements and stay alert."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, go to the nearest police station to report it. If you stay at the scene of the accident, you may be vulnerable. Medical help after an accident is likely to be limited, especially outside of Bamako."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fuel shortages"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently a fuel shortage in Mali. Where fuel is available, there can often be long lines and in many parts of the country the price of fuel has increased. Plan ahead to make sure you can reach your destination."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Inbound and outbound flights, including international flights, can be cancelled at short notice or diverted to an alternative location. Monitor messages from your carrier, and be prepared to make arrangements to stay overnight in a safe location."]},{"k":"p","s":["The security at Bamako airport is heavy, and guards search your vehicle before you enter the airport. Scammers posing as taxi drivers and guides operate around the airport – only use pre-arranged transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Mali outside of Bamako are extremely dangerous. Terrorist groups have repeatedly shelled Timbuktu airport since August 2023."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season in Mali is from June to October. Heavy rains can cause floods and landslides. Monitor local weather reports and expect difficulties when travelling to affected areas during this season."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["The emergency number is 15 but emergency response capacity is very limited. Take local advice and arrange your own transport to a medical centre or hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Mali","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/140/mali#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Mali,","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/140/mali"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["typhoid and cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["rabies"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["meningitis"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should drink only boiled or bottled water, and avoid ice in drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies are easily identifiable throughout Bamako. The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or purchased in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Mali"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Mali are very limited. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Mali","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mali-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Mali"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency response capacity is very limited. If no help is available, take local advice and arrange your own transport locally."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 17"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 15"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 18"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Mali"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Mali"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Mali"]," in Mali"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Mali","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mali-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Mali","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mali-prisoners-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/mali/british-embassy-bamako"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":21510,"change":"Updated information about recent terrorist attacks in Mali (‘Safety and security’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/flight-of-the-conchords-return-to-nz-stages-after-14-years-away-but-wellington-is-still-obviously-home-296280":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"2c983bf4bd1c1ffe54aa81ca5c123d5f0cbce962ac646c29a224554a300c28eb","read":"https://theconversation.com/flight-of-the-conchords-return-to-nz-stages-after-14-years-away-but-wellington-is-still-obviously-home-296280","bytes":180598,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Flight of the Conchords return to NZ stages after 14 years away – but Wellington is still obviously home","by":[{"n":"David Simes","r":"Teaching Assistant and Researcher, Te Whare Ngangahau – Theatre and Performance Studies, Te Herenga Waka — Victoria University of Wellington"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T23:22:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["What is it about a musical comedy duo that formed in 1998 and describes itself as Aotearoa New Zealand’s “fourth most popular comedy folk duo” that remains so appealing?"]},{"k":"p","s":["After 14 years away from New Zealand stages, Flight of the Conchords – Bret McKenzie and Jemaine Clement – have returned for a sold-out tour."]},{"k":"p","s":["Performing before a capacity crowd as they begin the tour in Wellington, McKenzie and Clement are in fine form. Even when they can’t remember every lyric or musical cue, they have the audience wrapped around their fingers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Each mistake humanises them (ironically, considering the first song has them performing as ",["robots","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NI9nopaieEc"],"). Mistakes are seemingly part of the act."]},{"k":"p","s":["Through deadpan delivery and deliberately understated performances, the duo have cultivated the impression that they are ordinary people who have somehow wandered onto an international stage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their appeal comes from their ability to make extraordinary success feel entirely unpretentious."]},{"k":"h","s":["Simply two friends"]},{"k":"p","s":["At their core, Flight of the Conchords are simply two friends playing instruments and making each other laugh. The audience responds because they recognise something of themselves in that dynamic."]},{"k":"p","s":["That familiarity is part of what has made them endure."]},{"k":"p","s":["They’ve also avoided becoming trapped simply as musical comedians."]},{"k":"p","s":["Classic songs such as Business Time, The Most Beautiful Girl (In the Room), and Inner City Pressure, which found global success on their HBO sitcom (2007–09) and 2008 album, remain funny some 20 years after first being written, simply because they target human emotion and situations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Part of the community"]},{"k":"p","s":["For anyone living in Wellington, seeing McKenzie or Clement around town is hardly unusual, since they both still call the city home. Despite winning a Grammy award, an ",["Academy Award","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8sIBz-rEEW8"]," for McKenzie, and numerous high-profile international acting roles for Clement, both remain strongly associated with the city that helped launch their careers."]},{"k":"p","s":["This connection is evident."]},{"k":"p","s":["At one point, Clement jokes the performance was “the most convenient gig” they “have ever done”. Yet the gig feels like a genuine celebration of Wellington itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two of the city’s best-known street performers were brought onstage during the set: ",["Woody","https://www.stuff.co.nz/entertainment/arts/130612203/my-wellington-how-a-saxophoneplaying-tree-entertains-the-capital"],", the saxophonist who performs dressed as a tree; and ",["King Homeboy","https://www.stuff.co.nz/nz-news/360910267/hip-hop-champ-hits-mute-beatboxing-after-brain-surgery"],", the world champion beatboxer who has entertained crowds on Cuba Street for years."]},{"k":"p","s":["They received some of the loudest applause of the night – especially King Homeboy, who gets a standing ovation for his beatboxing during Hiphopopotamus vs Rhymenoceros."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite international success, Flight of the Conchords still see themselves as products of a particular place and community."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was not simply a concert taking place in Wellington. It was a concert that could only happen in Wellington."]},{"k":"h","s":["The ingredients for success"]},{"k":"p","s":["The city played a crucial role in the duo’s rise. McKenzie and Clement met while studying at Victoria University of Wellington and developed their early work through venues such as ",["BATS Theatre","https://www.stuff.co.nz/dominion-post/news/wellington/9918736/Conchords-pair-go-in-to-bat-for-theatre"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["They emerged from an arts sector that was hardly overflowing with money. Their success was not the result of lavish public investment or a carefully designed talent program. Instead, they benefited from something less tangible: time and space to experiment and play."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wellington in the ",["late 1990s and early 2000s offered","https://doi.org/10.1080/07352166.2024.2345651"]," relatively affordable living costs, accessible performance venues, and pathways that allowed emerging artists to develop unconventional work before finding larger audiences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those conditions are getting harder and harder to maintain. Recent government budgets have ",["reduced spending across a number of cultural organisations","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/business/752841/creative-nz-to-cut-a-third-of-workforce"],", while artists and venues face rising costs and increasing competition for a ",["limited number of funding opportunities","https://thespinoff.co.nz/culture/02-08-2026/has-the-arts-sector-ever-done-it-this-hard"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ministry for Culture and Heritage’s own ",["summary of the 2024 budget","https://www.mch.govt.nz/publications/budget-2024"]," outlines reductions facing multiple cultural agencies. But if a 28-year-old comedy duo can sell out venues across the country, it is proof that this is misaligned."]},{"k":"p","s":["New Zealander’s want to see our art on stages. It just needs ",["proper funding","https://theconversation.com/why-a-chronically-underfunded-arts-sector-will-make-nz-poorer-and-duller-289788"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The lesson of Flight of the Conchords is not that New Zealand once funded the arts generously. It is that even a modest arts ecosystem can produce remarkable talent when emerging artists have opportunities to experiment, fail and try again."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whether today’s environment provides these same opportunities is a question worth asking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Welcome home"]},{"k":"p","s":["After nearly three decades, countless side projects, international television success, award winds and individual careers that easily could have pulled them in different directions, McKenzie and Clement retain the chemistry that made audiences fall in love with them in the first place."]},{"k":"p","s":["Watching them perform feels less like watching global stars and more like watching those two university flatmates continue a joke they started ages ago."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was rust. As McKenzie said, they have “potential” to be great. There were moments where things threatened to fall apart."]},{"k":"p","s":["But perhaps that is the point."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flight of the Conchords have never succeeded despite their imperfections, but rather, because of them. And judging by the sell-out crowds welcoming them home to thunderous applause and huge laughs, New Zealand wouldn’t have it any other way."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flight of the Conchords are touring Aotearoa New Zealand until November 21."]}],"chars":5311},"https://theconversation.com/i-study-polling-failures-this-time-pollsters-were-mostly-right-if-not-precise-295433":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"b58aabcd658ae51b291b304d6d5118e4728cba659d70683c30802e4b7c8c3057","read":"https://theconversation.com/i-study-polling-failures-this-time-pollsters-were-mostly-right-if-not-precise-295433","bytes":183714,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"I study polling failures – this time, pollsters were mostly right, if not precise","by":[{"n":"W Joseph Campbell","r":"Professor Emeritus of Communication, American University School of Communication"}],"pub":"2026-11-04T23:10:15Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The crucial test for preelection polls is whether they broadly indicate ",["how voters are likely to decide","https://x.com/Mark_Penn/status/2117882684751884343"],". By that fundamental measure, the 2026 midterm polls largely succeeded in anticipating outcomes on Election Day."]},{"k":"p","s":["If somewhat tentatively, the polls overall had been ",["signaling important gains for Democrats","https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/pretty-much-every-poll-is-good-for-democrats-now.html"],". And that is what voting produced."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was, perhaps, polling’s most reassuring performance since ",["accurately anticipating Barack Obama’s presidential election","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/president/general/2008/mccain-vs-obama"]," in 2008, an outcome cited in my book, ",["“Lost in a Gallup: Polling Failure in U.S. Presidential Elections.”","https://www.ucpress.edu/books/lost-in-a-gallup/paper"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Two truisms confirmed"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not to say the 2026 preelection polls offered precision estimates before returns poured in. They appear to have ",["underestimated support for Democratic candidates","https://www.foxnews.com/politics/america-saw-blue-wave-coming-drastically-underestimated-extent-dem-tsunami"]," in some Senate races."]},{"k":"p","s":["But spot-on precision, while enviable, is not what polls can be expected to produce, considering the ",["many ways error can infiltrate","https://doi.org/10.1080/2330443X.2021.1971126"]," opinion surveys. Given their ",["checkered record in recent national elections","https://theconversation.com/no-cheery-time-for-election-pollsters-in-run-up-to-us-midterms-289772"],", pollsters and media analysts tended to couch their end-of-campaign assessments in ",["measured tentativeness","https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/2026/10/midterm-polls-error/688922/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, Nate Cohn, chief political analyst for The New York Times, ",["wrote just before the election","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/01/upshot/poll-times-siena-senate-midterms.html"]," that “it’s reasonable to wonder whether the polls might be overestimating Democratic strength yet again. This is a real possibility. President Trump’s supporters are relatively unlikely to respond to polls, which introduces the ever-present risk of a polling misfire.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["That risk was mostly unrealized, as Republican candidates were swept in ",["a red wipeout","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/04/us/politics/democratic-midterms-wipeout.html?unlocked_article_code=1.N1E.ia0W.PPiKVVjajWqm&smid=url"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 2026 polls tended to confirm the truism in American politics that midterms typically are rough on ",["candidates of the party that holds the presidency","https://spia.uga.edu/expert-voices/why-does-the-presidents-party-usually-lose-seats-in-midterm-elections/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another truism, again reaffirmed, is that a president’s approval ratings often are ",["useful in gauging","https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterm-election-news-2026/card/why-a-president-s-job-approval-rating-matters-L0iVimxfJYbbaYmFCB9O"]," the country’s mood before midterm elections. President Donald Trump’s preelection approval ratings ",["hovered at or below 40%","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/approval/donald-trump/approval-rating"],", according to survey data compiled by RealClearPolitics."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. war with Iran, launched by Trump, was ",["a major factor propelling the unenviable ratings","https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-acknowledges-iran-war-is-partly-to-blame-for-republican-losses-c3cf572e"],". The conflict went unresolved while ",["fuel prices surged","https://www.nbcnews.com/data-graphics/gas-prices-iran-war-state-national-cost-trump-rcna265835"],", bringing pain to consumers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those and other problems ",["prompted polling analyst Nate Silver","https://www.natesilver.net/p/its-judgment-day-for-trump-and-for"]," to write that Trump “almost seems to have a death wish in these midterms. And the one superpower he has – turning out low-propensity voters in presidential years, the sorts of voters who apparently are often missed by pollsters – has never really worked when Trump himself wasn’t on the ballot.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["And it didn’t work this time, either, even though throughout the campaign Trump encouraged supporters to ",["pretend his name was on the ballot","https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/6055367-trump-midterm-republican-voters-pretend-ballot/"]," and turn out to vote."]},{"k":"h","s":["Few polling misses"]},{"k":"p","s":["When examined closely, the polls delivered some disagreement in the days before the election. Pollsters offered ranges that, in some races, were sizable."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, was Republican Senate candidate Ken Paxton ",["up by 1 percentage point","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/texas/talarico-vs-paxton?card=159113&t=1793793732067"]," in Texas late in the campaign, or was he ",["down 7 points","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/texas/talarico-vs-paxton?card=159247&t=1793793767324"],"? Paxton lost by double digits to Democrat James Talarico, a margin that no pollster anticipated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Similarly, was long-serving Republican Sen. Susan Collins ",["ahead by 2 points","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/collins-vs-jackson?card=159347&t=1793794096175"]," in Maine or was she ",["losing by 9 points","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/collins-vs-jackson?card=159379&t=1793794123871"],"? The outcome was ",["closer to the latter reading","https://www.realclearpolitics.com/elections/live_results/2026/state/me/senate/"],", with Democrat Troy Jackson winning by more than six points."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Minnesota, was Democratic Senate candidate Peggy Flanagan ",["up by 14 points","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/minnesota/tafoya-vs-flanagan?card=158940&t=1793794316003"],", or by ",["just 2 points","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/senate/general/2026/minnesota/tafoya-vs-flanagan?card=159365&t=1793794357830"],"? With most votes counted by the day after the election, Flanagan’s margin of victory was ",["about 10 points","https://www.realclearpolitics.com/elections/live_results/2026/state/mn/senate/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such polling gaps in high-profile races offer a reminder to not focus on any single survey but, instead, to consider overall polling averages, which tend to remove or reduce the effects of outliers."]},{"k":"p","s":["None of this necessarily is to declare that pollsters have resolved their persistent ",["problems in sampling","https://aapor.org/polling-accuracy/"],", especially in interviewing hard-to-reach voters. But big polling misses ",["like that in the Texas governor’s race","https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/governor/general/2026/texas/abbott-vs-hinojosa"]," – where Democrat Gina Hinojosa won by double digits, although polls had shown Republican Gov. Greg Abbott ahead by a few points – were few this election cycle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the electorate’s broad inclinations were plainly if not precisely depicted."]},{"k":"p","s":["That outcome has to be heartening for pollsters, an often- ",["beleaguered","https://thehill.com/opinion/campaign/5586880-2024-election-polling-accuracy/"]," and ",["much-criticized","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/30/poll-americans-dont-trust-polls-01141115"]," cohort."]}],"chars":4265},"https://theconversation.com/south-africas-public-service-new-laws-aim-to-put-competent-people-in-charge-and-hold-them-to-account-292376":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"abdc2392ca39fc3f39ff80d8eaaf25d50a69eb599cbfd06f5e2347867c71dc15","read":"https://theconversation.com/south-africas-public-service-new-laws-aim-to-put-competent-people-in-charge-and-hold-them-to-account-292376","bytes":179364,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"South Africa’s public service: new laws aim to put competent people in charge and hold them to account","by":[{"n":"Busani Ngcaweni","r":"Director: Center for Public Policy and African Studies, University of Johannesburg"}],"pub":"2026-09-30T13:26:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["South Africa has been on a decades-long journey of reforming its public service. But serious problems persist."]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2026 the urgency for change was again underscored during ",["the Madlanga Commission of inquiry into corruption in the police and security forces","https://criminaljusticecommission.org.za/"],". In his ",["testimony","https://madlangacommission.co.za/witnesses/somadoda-fikeni"],", the chairperson of the ",["Public Service Commission","https://www.psc.gov.za/About"],", Somadoda Fikeni, lamented the state of governance and accountability. He said it sustained a culture of impunity in which officials directly benefited from the inconvenience suffered by members of the public. He called it the “ ",["political economy of inefficiency","https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/pscs-fikeni-highlights-existence-of-policies-but-failure-to-execute/"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["His testimony coincided with ",["the signing of the Public Service Commission Act into law","https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/public-service-commission-bill-enacted-law"]," by President Cyril Ramaphosa. The hope is that this will close gaps in accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new legislation completes a trio of public sector reforms. The other two pieces are the ",["Public Service Amendment Act 9 of 2025","https://www.dpsa.gov.za/dpsa2g/documents/acts%26regulations/PublicServiceAmendmentAct%2C%202026.pdf"]," and the ",["Public Administration Management Amendment Act 7 of 2025","https://www.dpsa.gov.za/dpsa2g/documents/acts%26regulations/PublicAdministrationManagement%20Act%2C%202025.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a researcher who also served as head the ",["National School of Government","https://www.thensg.gov.za/mandate/"],", where I led ",["the development of a national framework for the professionalisation of the public sector","https://www.thensg.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/NSG-A-NATIONAL-FRAMEWORK-TOWARDS-THE-PROFESSIONALISATION-OF-THE-PUBLIC-SECTOR.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["How significant is this moment for governance?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The three laws make important changes to the rules governing South Africa’s public administration system. These include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["who exercises administrative authority"]},{"k":"li","s":["how senior administrators are held accountable"]},{"k":"li","s":["how public servants are developed."]},{"k":"p","s":["They also set out how to manage conflicts of interest and how to protect the constitutional values governing public administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["New laws do not, by themselves, produce a capable and developmental state. South Africa has enough experience to know the distance that can exist between law and practice."]},{"k":"p","s":["The real test is whether these changes alter how authority is exercised, how appointments are made, how public servants are developed and how breaches of constitutional standards are dealt with."]},{"k":"h","s":["The foundation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The foundation for the new laws is ",["section 195 of the country’s constitution","https://www.gov.za/documents/constitution/constitution-republic-south-africa-1996-chapter-10-public-administration-07"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It requires the promotion and maintenance of “a high standard of professional ethics”, and that public resources be used efficiently, economically and effectively. It says public administration must be development-oriented and people’s needs must be addressed."]},{"k":"p","s":["It also requires accountability, transparency, fair and impartial service, good human resource management and a public administration broadly representative of the South African people."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Section 196","https://www.justice.gov.za/constitution/chp10.html"]," gives the ",["Public Service Commission","https://www.psc.gov.za/About"]," the power to promote the section 195 values and principles throughout the public service. They apply to all organs of state, not just public administration (national and provincial departments)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is where the work of the late ",["Stan Sangweni","https://sahistory.org.za/people/stanislaus-skumbuzo-mzilankatha-sangweni"]," becomes relevant to the new laws. He chaired the Public Service Commission from 1999 to 2009."]},{"k":"h","s":["The history"]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of what the new legislation does responds to the work of the commission under Sangweni’s leadership. The commission was concerned with how to protect merit in appointments, hold senior administrators accountable, manage the boundary between political authority and administration, make ethical conduct routine and ensure public administration was answerable to citizens."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was no legal certainty on its mandate in these areas until now, however."]},{"k":"p","s":["This I appreciated in 2020 when I was asked to develop the framework to make the civil service professional."]},{"k":"p","s":["Going back through the Public Service Commission archives, I found evidence that many of the questions confronting the drafting team had been examined during Sangweni’s tenure. This reinforced the fact that institutional memory is a form of state capability. A state that keeps starting again condemns each generation of public servants to rediscover problems that others have already studied."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a longer history connecting this work of Sangweni to the present reforms. ",["The National Development Plan: Vision 2030","https://www.gov.za/sites/default/files/gcis_document/201409/ndp-2030-our-future-make-it-workr.pdf"]," chapter on building a capable and developmental state called for a professional public service, stronger technical and specialist skills, and clearer delegation, accountability and oversight."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Professionalisation Framework","https://www.thensg.gov.za/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/NATIONAL-FRAMEWORK-BOOKLET.pdf"],", published in 2022, also addressed how:"]},{"k":"li","s":["people enter the public sector"]},{"k":"li","s":["senior appointments should become more merit-based and technically rigorous"]},{"k":"li","s":["public servants should be inducted, developed, assessed and supported throughout their careers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The framework set the policy basis for the legislative process. The result is the three laws that have now been passed."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s been put in place"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Public Service Amendment Act changes the balance of authority inside departments. Heads of department will now have some powers that used to belong to ministers, including power to make appointments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political executives are still responsible for political leadership, policy and strategic direction. Heads of department have clearer administrative responsibilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["This raises the stakes around who becomes a head of department. If they have more authority, there must be greater confidence in the integrity and professional rigour of their appointment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Public Administration Management Amendment Act addresses another part of the problem. It strengthens the statutory position of the ",["National School of Government","https://www.thensg.gov.za/"]," and the basis for education, training, assessment and professional development across public administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new law also strengthens integrity provisions, like restrictions on employees doing business with the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Public Service Commission Act ",["strengthens the commission itself","https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/public-service-commission-bill-enacted-law"],", through a secretariat. It also extends its mandate to municipalities and public entities. This is closer to the idea of a single public administration system."]},{"k":"h","s":["Seen as a whole"]},{"k":"p","s":["The significance of these reforms becomes clearer when they are considered together."]},{"k":"p","s":["Administrative authority is being moved closer to those who must account for what departments do. Senior appointments are to be more professional. The machinery for professional education and development is being strengthened. Integrity provisions are being tightened. Most importantly, the constitutional institution charged with promoting the values of section 195 is being strengthened and given wider reach."]},{"k":"p","s":["South Africa will hold ",["local government elections on 4 November","https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/lge-president-ramaphosa-declares-4-november-public-holiday"],". The South African Local Government Association, the National School of Government, provincial governments and other institutions preparing the induction of incoming councillors and municipal executives will have to incorporate the new legal framework into those programmes."]}],"chars":6559},"https://theconversation.com/beau-lamarre-condon-has-been-found-guilty-of-two-murders-legal-experts-explain-why-296148":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-25T07:09Z","sha":"707fba471ff59a084d379f6fce146226ebd1270887981d5c0ae061d96f2d8146","read":"https://theconversation.com/beau-lamarre-condon-has-been-found-guilty-of-two-murders-legal-experts-explain-why-296148","bytes":180567,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Beau Lamarre-Condon has been found guilty of two murders. Legal experts explain why","by":[{"n":"Ben Livings","r":"Associate Professor in Criminal Law and Criminal Justice, Adelaide University"},{"n":"Rick Sarre","r":"Emeritus Professor in Law and Criminal Justice, Adelaide University"}],"pub":"2026-11-25T06:05:49Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The jury in Beau Lamarre-Condon’s trial at the New South Wales Supreme Court today found the former police officer ",["guilty","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-25/beau-lamarre-condon-verdict-found-guilty-jesse-baird-luke-davies/107420442"]," of two counts of murder."]},{"k":"p","s":["He was also found guilty of the offence of breaking and entering a house and committing a serious indictable offence (in this case, stealing)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The verdict follows a nine-week trial over the 2024 deaths of Jesse Baird and Luke Davies. Here’s how the case played out."]},{"k":"h","s":["What happened?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The events covered in the trial took place in February 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was undisputed at trial that Lamarre-Condon had gone to Paddington, a suburb of inner Sydney, to the home of Baird, a man with whom he had had a casual relationship that had ended three months earlier."]},{"k":"p","s":["There, Lamarre-Condon shot Baird and his new partner, Davies, using his police issue handgun."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite admitting to the killing, Lamarre-Condon pleaded not guilty to all charges. He claimed he had acted in self-defence."]},{"k":"h","s":["The evidence considered by the jury"]},{"k":"p","s":["A defendant in a criminal trial is not required to give evidence. In this case, Lamarre-Condon chose to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["His evidence was that he had gone to Baird’s house to collect some of his own belongings, which he had forgotten to remove following the end of their relationship."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lamarre-Condon claimed he arrived wearing an Uber Eats ",["delivery driver outfit","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/26/disguised-as-an-uber-eats-driver-beau-lamarre-condon-entered-his-exs-home-moments-later-three-gun-shots-rung-out-ntwnfb"]," to avoid any accusation that he was stalking or harassing Baird. He maintained Baird had previously told him where he could find a key to the house."]},{"k":"p","s":["His account was that, on the day of the killings, Baird was in his kitchen holding a knife, and did not recognise him because of the bicycle helmet he was wearing. A struggle ensued."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lamarre-Condon claimed he was forced to defend himself. He told the jury he shot Baird first to disarm him and a second time accidentally as they fell to the floor."]},{"k":"p","s":["He gave evidence of a second struggle with Davies in the hallway, claiming Davies had picked up the gun and accidentally shot himself during that second struggle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lamarre-Condon then went about trying to conceal the killings. ",["He admitted to disposing","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-24/beau-lamarre-condon-sydney-murder-trial-defence-closing-argument/107420402"]," of the victims’ bloodied belongings in a skip bin some 30 kilometres from the murder scene and put their bodies in surfboard bags."]},{"k":"p","s":["He used a hire van as transport and initially attempted to sink the bodies in a Bungonia dam, but ultimately disposed of them at a nearby monastery. He was accompanied by a friend who has been granted anonymity and been assured she would not face prosecution as a condition of giving evidence."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Four days after","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/11/24/world/australia-lamarre-condon-verdict-intl-hnk"]," the killings, Lamarre-Condon handed himself in to Bondi police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lamarre-Condon’s legal team relied on the disorganised nature of the cover-up and the lack of preparation of events post-killing to support Lamarre-Condon’s case for self-defence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Intent to kill"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although a murder conviction does not require proof of motive or premeditation, it does require proof of intent. Where the accused argues self-defence, as in this case, it is the job of the prosecution to show this is not a reasonable possibility."]},{"k":"p","s":["The prosecution put forward evidence that Lamarre-Condon had become infatuated with Baird following their relationship. They told the court he had stalked Baird, monitored his movements using the app Snapchat and had broken into Baird’s home on multiple occasions before the fateful events in February 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["In handing down guilty verdicts, the jury agreed with the prosecution’s submission that there was intent and no credible suggestion of self-defence. They did not believe the accused’s contrary version of events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their verdicts of guilt were ",["delivered unanimously","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-25/nsw-beau-lamarre-condon-verdict-live-jesse-baird-luke-davies/107419836"]," after just two hours of deliberation, which is, on any account, a very quick turn-around from a trial of this length."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lamarre-Condon is expected to be sentenced by Justice Natalie Adams on March 11 next year. As part of that process, she will consider victim impact statements."]},{"k":"h","s":["What sentences are available to the judge?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["The murder convictions","https://sentencingcouncil.nsw.gov.au/about-sentencing/cases-of-interest/murder.html"]," each have a maximum penalty of ",["life imprisonment","https://www5.austlii.edu.au/au/legisconsol_act/ca190082/s19a.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The offence of breaking and entering a house and committing a serious indictable offence has a ",["maximum penalty","https://www5.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/nsw/consol_act/ca190082/s105a.html"]," of 14 years imprisonment, or up to 25 years if there are circumstances of “special aggravation”."]},{"k":"p","s":["When a judge imposes a sentence for murder in NSW, the standard non-parole period is ",["20 years","https://www.judcom.nsw.gov.au/publications/benchbks/sentencing/appendix_a.html"],". This increases to 25 years where the victim is a current or former intimate partner."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, these are only starting points for the judge’s consideration in sentencing. Given the seriousness and existence of multiple offences in this case, it is open to the judge to impose a sentence that will mean Lamarre-Condon will spend the rest of his life in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whatever the outcome of Justice Adams’ deliberations, there is little doubt Lamarre-Condon can expect to spend a very long time behind bars."]},{"k":"p","s":["The National Sexual Assault, Family and Domestic Violence Counselling Line – 1800 RESPECT (1800 737 732) – is available 24 hours a day, seven days a week for any Australian who has experienced, or is at risk of, family and domestic violence and/or sexual assault."]}],"chars":5006}};
